cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
title: "ANADEF: Alarm-based Nested-permutation Assessment of Dual-parameter Earthquake Forecasting"
version: 2.1.0
abstract: >-
  A protocol and open implementation for testing whether a secondary spatial predictor, here the
  Gutenberg-Richter b-value field, adds forecasting information beyond the background seismicity rate.
  Its central element is a nested permutation test in which the secondary threshold is re-optimised
  inside every null realisation, so that the advantage conferred by threshold calibration enters the
  null distribution instead of inflating the result.
